{
 "id": "arnio-pr1340",
 "repo": "im-anishraj/arnio",
 "base_ref": "v1.20.0",
 "base_commit": "2e3fe965c963d45ae156c32ef230c7eb7a29a777",
 "issue": 1332,
 "issue_title": "Bug:  Memory Exhaustion (OOM) via unbounded source.read() in _materialize_csv_input()",
 "issue_body": "### What happened?\n\nIn `arnio/io.py`, the `_materialize_csv_input()` function converts file-like objects (e.g., `io.StringIO` or raw streams) into temporary files on disk so the C++ backend can read them. However, it reads the **entire contents** of the stream into memory at once using `source.read()` without chunking. If a user passes a large stream (like a multi-gigabyte network socket stream), Arnio attempts to allocate gigabytes of contiguous RAM just to hold the string. This defeats the purpose of chunked processing and instantly crashes the Python process with a `MemoryError`.\n\n### Area\n\nCSV parser / read_csv / scan_csv\n\n### Minimal reproduction\n\nimport arnio as ar\nimport io\n\n# Simulate a massive file stream that generates data on the fly\nclass MassiveStream(io.StringIO):\n    def read(self, size=-1):\n        # A real implementation would yield chunks, \n        # but Arnio currently forces size=-1 (read all at once)\n        return \"a,b,c\\n1,2,3\\n\" * 10_000_000 \n\nstream = MassiveStream()\n\n# This immediately causes an OOM / MemoryError because \n# arnio tries to load the entire stream into a single string\n# inside _materialize_csv_input() before chunking begins\nframe = ar.read_csv_chunked(stream, chunksize=10_000)\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nArnio should stream the file-like object in small chunks (e.g., 8192 bytes at a time) directly into the `NamedTemporaryFile` on disk. This would keep memory usage extremely low and constant, allowing `read_csv_chunked()` to properly handle infinitely large streams without OOM crashes.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 1, in <module>\n  File \"/path/to/arnio/io.py\", line 353, in _materialize_csv_input\n    content = source.read()\nMemoryError\n\n### Impact\n\nBlocks installation or import\n\n### Arnio version\n\n1.1.0\n\n### Install method\n\nbuilt from source or pip install arnio\n\n### Operating System\n\nWindows\n\n### Python version\n\n3.12.4\n\n### Environment details\n\n```shell\n**Proposed Fix in `arnio/io.py`**:\nInstead of `content = source.read()`, the file writing loop should be:\n\ntmp = tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(mode=\"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\", suffix=\".csv\", delete=False)\ntry:\n    while True:\n        chunk = source.read(8192)\n        if not chunk:\n            break\n        tmp.write(chunk)\n    tmp.close()\n    return tmp.name, True\nexcept Exception:\n    os.unlink(tmp.name)\n    raise\n```\n\n### Pre-flight checks\n\n- [x] I searched existing issues and did not find a duplicate.\n- [x] I included a minimal reproduction or explained why one is not possible.\n\n### Additional context\n\nPlease assign this issue to me, I would love to work on the fix!",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/im-anishraj/arnio/issues/1332",
 "pr": 1340,
 "pr_title": "fix: harden file-like CSV inputs and sklearn feature names",
 "pr_body": "## Summary\n- copy text file-like CSV inputs to temporary files in bounded chunks instead of one unbounded `read()` call\n- allow `read_csv_chunked()` to accept text file-like inputs with the same bounded-copy path\n- cache ArnioCleaner output feature names after transform so sklearn pipelines see dropped/renamed columns correctly\n- add regression coverage for bounded file-like reads and sklearn `get_feature_names_out()` behavior\n\n## Linked issues\nCloses #1332\nCloses #1335\n\nNote: #1337 is intentionally not closed here. Duplicate CSV header auto-mangling is a maintainer/API decision because Arnio currently rejects duplicate headers by design.\n\n## Local verification\n- `ruff check arnio/io.py arnio/integrations/sklearn.py tests/test_csv.py tests/test_sklearn.py`\n- `black --check arnio/io.py arnio/integrations/sklearn.py tests/test_csv.py tests/test_sklearn.py`\n- `python -m py_compile arnio/io.py arnio/integrations/sklearn.py tests/test_csv.py tests/test_sklearn.py`\n- `git diff --check`\n\nFull native pytest is blocked in this local shell because `_arnio_cpp` is not compiled and MSVC `cl`/`nmake` are not on PATH. GitHub Actions should provide the native matrix verification.",
